    "diagnosis": "Pathogenesis of von Hippel&ndash;Lindau syndrome",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<strong>A</strong>&nbsp;The &beta; domain of VHL protein interacts with HIF1&alpha;, whereas the &alpha; domain interacts with other partners of the VHL protein complex. In von Hippel&ndash;Lindau syndrome, alterations in the &alpha; domain prevent the formation of a functional VHL protein complex. <strong>B</strong>&nbsp;In normoxia, the VHL complex binds to HIF1&alpha; and promotes ubiquitination and proteasomal degradation in an oxygen-dependent manner. In hypoxia, binding of VHL protein to HIF1&alpha; is impaired, resulting in the accumulation of HIF1&alpha; and increased activation of target genes. In von Hippel&ndash;Lindau syndrome, HIF1&alpha; accumulation results from failed binding of HIF1&alpha; to the dysfunctional VHL protein complex. <strong>C</strong>&nbsp;HIF accumulation in haemangioblastoma stromal tumour cells leads to altered gene expression of HIF-responsive genes and results in increased vascularization due to angiogenesis and vasculogenesis; cyst formation due to increased vascular permeability; and metabolic adaptation, growth stimulation, extramedullary haematopoiesis, and lipid deposition (clear cell phenotype).",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Plate KH<br />and<br />Susanne Berger, graphical-abstracts.com",
